invalid-define-component.js:7:15 lint/nursery/noVueUndeclaredEmits ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The event close is emitted, but the component doesn't declare it.
  
    5 │ 	methods: {
    6 │ 		close() {
  > 7 │ 			this.$emit("close");
      │ 			           ^^^^^^^
    8 │ 		},
    9 │ 	},
  
  i Vue also adds a listener for an undeclared event to the root element of the component. If that element sends a native event with the same name, such as click, the listener runs twice.
  
  i Add close to the emits option or to the defineEmits() call of the component.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

